# Accepted findings from the Trivy security scan, each with the reason.
# Anything NOT listed here fails the CI build.

# Egress to 0.0.0.0/0 (ports 443 and 80 only): the server must reach AWS APIs, container
# registries and Ubuntu mirrors, whose IPs change. Inbound is fully closed. VPC endpoints
# would cost about $7/month each.
AWS-0104

# S3 bucket and SNS topic use AWS-managed encryption keys instead of customer-managed KMS
# keys ($1/month each). Data is still encrypted at rest; fine for a demo project.
AWS-0132
AWS-0136

# The bucket only holds a rebuildable bundle whose name is its own SHA-256,
# so versioning and access logging add cost without value.
AWS-0089
AWS-0090

# The health check is defined in docker-compose.yml, because this image also runs the load generator.
DS-0026
